   "text": {
    "L1": "A tiling covers a floor with no gaps and no overlaps.",
    "L2": "At every corner, the tile angles must add to exactly 360 degrees.",
    "L3": "A regular polygon tiles on its own when its angle divides 360 degrees exactly.",
    "L4": "Triangles, squares, and regular hexagons pass this test: six, four, or three fit around a corner.",
    "L5": "A regular pentagon has angle 108 degrees. Three make 324 degrees, leaving a 36-degree gap.",
    "L6": "So not every regular polygon tiles on its own. But any quadrilateral can tile because its four angles add to 360 degrees.",
    "L7": "To test a shape, find its angle and divide 360 by it. A whole number means no gap or overlap.",
    "L8": "Now find the missing angle at this corner: 120 degrees, 90 degrees, 80 degrees, and one more angle."
   },
